[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "2607241800", :adr/title "cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger -- loan-based commitment-ledger actor bridging self-registered businesses to institutional/individual lenders, deliberately not ISIC-coded", :adr/status :accepted, :adr/date "2026-07-24", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/related ["gftdcojp/cloud-itonami/docs/adr/0013-open-business-self-registration.md" "gftdcojp/cloud-itonami/docs/adr/0028-ma-matching-deal-flow.md" "2607061700-cloud-itonami-vc-fund-blueprint" "2607141700-cloud-itonami-isic-6493-factoring-actor" "cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md"], :adr/repo-created "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger", :adr/pattern "sealed Commitment-LLM advisor + independent CommitmentLedgerGovernor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on cloud-itonami-isic-6492 (Store/Registry/Governor/Phase/Advisor/Operation/Sim shape) and cloud-itonami-isic-6493 (two-actuation, no-WASM-safety-kernel shape); registered directly at :implemented", :adr/why-not-isic-coded "cross-cutting matching/auxiliary capability layered on gftdcojp/cloud-itonami ADR-0013 self-registration, not an industry vertical; the financial-services ISIC codes this actor is closest to (6491/6492/6493/6495/6499/6419/6619/6611/6612) are already claimed by sibling actors in this fleet, and this actor does not itself grant credit, factor receivables, or hold deposits", :adr/auxiliary-non-balance-sheet-boundary "this actor does NOT move money itself -- no account/ledger balance, no fund custody, no payment-gateway/processor integration anywhere in the codebase; every commit is a DRAFT authorization record (unsigned certificate, issued_by_registry false, status draft-unsigned), actual disbursement delegated to cloud-itonami-isic-6492/cloud-itonami-isic-6419/external rails", :adr/two-actuation-commitment-ledger "two actuation events (:actuation/commitment-record, :actuation/tranche-release), both permanently excluded from every phases :auto set, matching cloud-itonami-isic-6493 multi-actuation shape; commitment-record is the first commit (matched lender + terms + personal pledge), tranche-release is a later independent run gated on milestone evidence and a dedicated double-release guard", :adr/ten-hard-checks-commitment-record "spec-basis-missing?, institutional-lender-license-not-verified?, rate-ceiling-exceeded? (\u5229\u606f\u5236\u9650\u6cd5 tiers 20%/18%/15%), individual-lender-not-interest-free?, individual-lender-principal-exceeds-cap? (\u00a5100,000), individual-lender-loan-count-exceeds-threshold? (3+ prior committed records), capacity-ratio-exceeded? (>0.43), equity-language-detected?, personal-pledge-incomplete? (distinctive check), borrower-not-self-registered? (reference well-formedness only, no live HTTP integration in V1)", :adr/distinctive-check-commitment-ledger "personal-pledge-incomplete-violations: every application must carry a complete, NON-FINANCIAL personal pledge (milestone-report-cadence, mentor-checkin-commitment, progress-report-obligation) before a commitment can ever be recorded -- a human accountability commitment gating a financial actuation, novel to this fleet check-family taxonomy", :adr/individual-lender-safeguards-not-legal-advice "three individual-lender-specific checks (interest-free-only, \u00a5100,000 principal cap, 3-loan-count threshold) are explicitly documented as CONSERVATIVE SOFTWARE PROXIES for \u8ca8\u91d1\u696d\u6cd5 \u300c\u696d\u3068\u3057\u3066\u300d (acting-as-a-business) regulatory risk, NOT a legal bright line and NOT legal advice; a real deployment operator should treat the threshold as configurable and consult actual legal counsel", :adr/v1-lending-only-scope "owner instruction: V1 models loans only, no equity/investment/cap table; equity-language-detected-violations mirrors cloud_itonami.funding/guard-non-equity! token-for-token (re-implemented locally, no shared code across the repo boundary, matching the VC-fund-trio funding.cljc concept-reuse convention)", :adr/test-status-commitment-ledger "61 tests / 242 assertions, lint clean (clj-kondo 0 errors/0 warnings), demo (clojure -M:dev:run) verified end-to-end: one clean lifecycle through both actuations plus the double-release guard and a missing-milestone-evidence hold, plus ALL TEN :commitment/record HARD-hold scenarios, none of which ever reach a human", :adr/west-pin-bookkeeping-commitment-ledger "manifest/repos.edn :extra-projects gained one new entry; manifest/west.yml pin generated via nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger (5-line single-entry diff), server-side pin-verified against pushed main tip 85eda9ced1568f88d0e5499f2fb49be12c6a3ec9; nbb scripts/west-orphan-audit.cljs --blocking exit 0", :adr/no-industry-registry-entry "since this actor is deliberately not ISIC-coded, it is NOT added to kotoba-lang/industry\u2019s registry the way every cloud-itonami-isic-* actor is; fleet-wide :implemented ISIC-registry counts are unchanged by this registration -- this actor is tracked solely via manifest/west.yml + this ADR", :adr/body "# ADR-2607241800: `cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger` -- new actor, registered directly at `:implemented`\n\n- Status: Accepted (2026-07-24)\n- Related: `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami` ADR-0013 (open-business self-registration\n  -- the borrower identity this actor's `:borrower-org-repo`/`:borrower-did`\n  fields reference); `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami` ADR-0028 (M&A matching deal\n  flow -- another cross-cutting matching capability on the same platform,\n  precedent for a matching layer that is not itself an ISIC vertical);\n  `90-docs/adr/2607061700-cloud-itonami-vc-fund-blueprint.edn` (the\n  `:capital-call/issue`-style staged-release actuation pattern this\n  actor's own two-stage `:commitment/record` -> `:commitment/tranche-\n  release` actuation is analogous to); `90-docs/adr/2607141700-cloud-\n  itonami-isic-6493-factoring-actor.edn` (the two-actuation, no-WASM-\n  safety-kernel template this build follows most directly);\n  `cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (the\n  authoritative repo-level architecture record for this actor -- this\n  superproject ADR records the fleet-level context, ISIC non-coding\n  rationale, and registry/manifest bookkeeping)\n\n## Context\n\n`cloud-itonami`'s open-business self-registration flow (ADR-0013 in\n`gftdcojp/cloud-itonami`) lets a third party claim an independent\n`{org}/{repo}` tenant and appear in the public open-business registry,\ngiving a young entrepreneur's business a real, verifiable identity (an\n`org/repo` tenant plus a `did:key`). That flow stops at *registration*\n-- it does not connect a registered business to any form of capital.\n\nThe owner asked for a \"commitment ledger\": a governed actor that\nbridges a self-registered business to LOAN-BASED (explicitly NOT\nequity/investment) financial support from two distinct kinds of\nlender -- institutional (banks, licensed lending institutions) and\nindividual (a person lending directly, not a licensed institution,\ncarrying materially different regulatory risk under 貸金業法's\n「業として」(acting as a business) licensing threshold). V1 scope is\nlending only, per explicit owner instruction; this is a real,\nload-bearing scope boundary enforced by a HARD governor check\n(`equity-language-detected-violations`), not a README disclaimer.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. `cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger` is registered as a new repository\n   (public, AGPL-3.0-or-later, matching every `cloud-itonami` sibling's\n   visibility) with **Commitment-LLM ⊣ CommitmentLedgerGovernor** --\n   `commitledger.*` namespaces, modeled closely on `cloud-itonami-isic-\n   6492`'s Store/Registry/Governor/Phase/Advisor/Operation/Sim shape\n   (the closest operational template: single-application-entity Store,\n   ground-truth-recompute affordability/capacity-ratio check) and\n   `cloud-itonami-isic-6493`'s two-actuation, no-WASM-safety-kernel\n   shape (the template for this build's TWO actuation events decided\n   directly in idiomatic `.cljc`, matching the task's explicit \"no WASM\n   twin of any check\" scope boundary). Registered DIRECTLY at\n   `:implemented` (no intermediate `:blueprint` scaffold stage), since\n   it was built and tested end-to-end before registration -- the same\n   posture `cloud-itonami-isic-6493` and several recent post-blueprint-\n   tier-zero registrations in this registry have taken.\n2. **Why NOT ISIC-coded.** Unlike every `cloud-itonami-isic-*` actor,\n   this repo is deliberately not registered under an ISIC industry\n   code. It is a cross-cutting matching/auxiliary capability layered on\n   top of `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami`'s own self-registration flow\n   (ADR-0013), not an industry vertical. The financial-services ISIC\n   codes this actor's function is closest to are ALREADY claimed by\n   sibling actors in this fleet: `6491` financial leasing\n   (`cloud-itonami-isic-6491`), `6492`/`6495` credit granting, `6493`\n   factoring activities, `6499` other financial service activities\n   n.e.c. (the VC fund, `vcfund.*`), `6419` other monetary\n   intermediation, `6619` activities auxiliary to financial service\n   activities, `6611`/`6612` fund/security management. This actor does\n   not itself grant credit, does not itself factor receivables, and\n   does not itself hold deposits or move money -- it matches a\n   self-registered business to a lender and records the authorization;\n   the real financial act is always delegated downstream to one of\n   those already-ISIC-coded siblings or an external rail.\n3. **Auxiliary, non-balance-sheet design boundary.** This actor does\n   NOT move money itself. `commitledger.registry/register-commitment`/\n   `register-tranche-release` build DRAFT records (unsigned\n   certificates, `\"issued_by_registry\" false`, `\"status\"\n   \"draft-unsigned\"` -- the same discipline `credit.registry`'s and\n   `factoring.registry`'s own draft-record constructors already\n   establish). No account/ledger balance, no fund custody, no\n   payment-gateway/processor integration exists anywhere in this\n   codebase. Actual disbursement is explicitly delegated to\n   `cloud-itonami-isic-6492`/`cloud-itonami-isic-6419`/external\n   disbursement rails, stated explicitly in the repo's own README and\n   ADR-0001.\n4. **Ten HARD checks gate `:commitment/record`** (the first actuation):\n   `spec-basis-missing?`, `institutional-lender-license-not-verified?`,\n   `rate-ceiling-exceeded?` (Japan's 利息制限法 tiered ceiling: <¥100,000\n   -> 20%, ¥100,000-¥1,000,000 -> 18%, >=¥1,000,000 -> 15%),\n   `individual-lender-not-interest-free?`,\n   `individual-lender-principal-exceeds-cap?` (¥100,000, the same\n   利息制限法 first-tier threshold reused as a conservative individual-\n   lender cap), `individual-lender-loan-count-exceeds-threshold?` (3 or\n   more prior COMMITTED records from the same individual lender's\n   did:key), `capacity-ratio-exceeded?` (>0.43, `credit.registry`'s\n   exact formula/constant re-implemented locally, never required across\n   the repo boundary), `equity-language-detected?` (token-for-token\n   mirror of `cloud_itonami.funding/equity-blocklist`, re-implemented\n   locally), `personal-pledge-incomplete?` (this actor's own\n   DISTINCTIVE check -- see Decision 6), and\n   `borrower-not-self-registered?` (V1: reference-field\n   well-formedness only, no live HTTP integration into `gftdcojp/\n   cloud-itonami`'s registry). TWO more HARD checks gate the\n   independent `:commitment/tranche-release` actuation:\n   `tranche-release-precondition-violations` (committed status +\n   in-range tranche-index + complete milestone evidence) and\n   `tranche-already-released-violations` (a DEDICATED boolean/set-\n   membership double-release guard, never inferred from `:status` --\n   mirroring `credit.governor`'s ADR-0001 Decision 5 / `factoring.\n   governor`'s `receivable-status-precondition-violations` lesson).\n5. **Individual-lender safeguards, honestly scoped as conservative\n   proxies, not legal advice.** An individual lender carries materially\n   different regulatory risk than a licensed institution under\n   貸金業法's 「業として」(acting as a business) threshold. This actor's\n   three individual-lender-specific checks (interest-free-only,\n   principal cap, loan-count threshold) are explicitly documented, in\n   both the repo's `commitledger.registry` and `commitledger.governor`\n   docstrings AND this ADR, as CONSERVATIVE SOFTWARE PROXIES for that\n   regulatory risk -- NOT a legal bright line, and NOT legal advice. The\n   loan-count threshold (3) in particular is this actor's own\n   conservative default, not a number the statute itself draws a hard\n   line at; a real deployment's operator should treat it as\n   configurable and consult actual legal counsel for the applicable\n   jurisdiction.\n6. **The distinctive check.** `personal-pledge-incomplete-violations`\n   is this actor's own novel contribution to the fleet's check-family\n   taxonomy: every application must carry a complete, NON-FINANCIAL\n   personal pledge (`:milestone-report-cadence`, `:mentor-checkin-\n   commitment`, `:progress-report-obligation`) before a commitment can\n   ever be recorded -- a human accountability commitment, not a\n   financial covenant. No prior actor in this fleet gates a financial\n   actuation on a purely human-accountability field like this.\n7. **Two-actuation shape, no WASM safety kernel.** Following\n   `cloud-itonami-isic-6493`'s (`factoring.*`) precedent rather than\n   `cloud-itonami-isic-6492`'s (`credit.*`): `commitledger.governor`\n   decides directly in idiomatic `.cljc`, with NO `kernels/gate.cljc`\n   WASM-compiled safety-kernel extraction -- an explicit, in-scope\n   decision for V1 (task instruction: no WASM twin of any check), not\n   an oversight. `:commitment/record` and `:commitment/tranche-release`\n   are both permanently excluded from every phase's `:auto` set by\n   construction, verified by dedicated structural-invariant tests, one\n   per actuation (`test/commitledger/phase_test.cljc`).\n8. **No `kotoba-lang/industry` ISIC registry entry** -- since this\n   actor is deliberately not ISIC-coded (Decision 2), it is not added\n   to `kotoba-lang/industry`'s registry the way every `cloud-itonami-\n   isic-*` actor is. Fleet-wide `:implemented` actor counts in this\n   registry are UNCHANGED by this registration; this actor is tracked\n   solely via `manifest/west.yml`/`manifest/repos.edn` (this ADR's own\n   west-pin bookkeeping, Decision 9) and this ADR.\n9. `manifest/repos.edn`'s `:extra-projects` vector gained one new entry\n   (`\"orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger\"`), and\n   `manifest/west.yml`'s pin was generated via `nbb scripts/gen-west-\n   manifest.cljs --entry cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger` (this repo's\n   CLAUDE.md's only sanctioned path for a new-entry registration): a\n   5-line, single-entry diff, server-side pin-verified against the\n   pushed `main` tip (`85eda9ced1568f88d0e5499f2fb49be12c6a3ec9`) before\n   being written. `nbb scripts/west-orphan-audit.cljs --blocking`\n   confirmed no `:local-root-broken` orphans were introduced.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) A self-registered young entrepreneur's business (ADR-0013) now\n  has a concrete, governed path to loan-based capital, with strict,\n  documented, load-bearing individual-lender safeguards -- real HARD\n  governor checks with dedicated tests, not README disclaimers.\n- (+) The fleet gains a genuinely new check-family contribution\n  (`personal-pledge-incomplete-violations`, a non-financial human-\n  accountability gate on a financial actuation) and a documented,\n  honestly-scoped \"conservative proxy, not legal bright line\" pattern\n  other actors facing similar ambiguous-legal-line domains can reuse.\n- (+) This ADR establishes a fleet precedent for a `cloud-itonami`\n  actor that is deliberately NOT ISIC-coded because its function is a\n  cross-cutting matching/auxiliary capability rather than an industry\n  vertical -- a distinct pattern from every prior `cloud-itonami-isic-*`\n  registration ADR in this superproject.\n- (+) The auxiliary, non-balance-sheet design boundary is explicit in\n  code and in this ADR: no account/ledger balance, no fund custody, no\n  payment-gateway integration anywhere in this codebase; every commit\n  is a DRAFT authorization record, never a real transfer.\n- (-) Still a proposal/authorization layer, not a real bank, not a real\n  licensed lender, and not real disbursement infrastructure -- actual\n  fund movement is entirely delegated to `cloud-itonami-isic-6492`/\n  `cloud-itonami-isic-6419`/external rails, none of which this repo\n  integrates with over a live network call.\n- (-) This R0 seeds only 4 jurisdictions (JPN, USA, GBR, DEU) with an\n  official spec-basis, out of ~194 worldwide;\n  `commitledger.facts/coverage` reports this honestly. The rate-\n  ceiling check applies Japan's 利息制限法 tiers universally rather than\n  per-jurisdiction -- an honest V1 simplification, documented in\n  `commitledger.registry`'s own docstring.\n- (-) No WASM/`.kotoba` safety-kernel twin of any check (explicit V1\n  scope boundary) -- `commitledger.governor`/`commitledger.phase`\n  decide directly in idiomatic `.cljc`.\n- (-) No live HTTP integration into `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami`'s\n  self-registration registry -- `borrower-not-self-registered-\n  violations` checks reference-field well-formedness only.\n- 61 tests / 242 assertions, lint-clean (clj-kondo, 0 errors/0\n  warnings), demo (`clojure -M:dev:run`) verified end-to-end: one clean\n  lifecycle through both actuations (application intake -> matched-\n  lender commitment record -> tranche-release, each escalating to\n  human approval) plus the double-release guard and a missing-\n  milestone-evidence hold, plus ALL TEN `:commitment/record` HARD-hold\n  scenarios (a jurisdiction with no spec-basis, an unverified\n  institutional license, a rate above the 利息制限法 ceiling, an\n  interest-bearing individual loan, an individual loan above the\n  principal cap, three clean individual loans from the SAME lender\n  followed by a fourth that trips the loan-count threshold, a\n  capacity-ratio breach, equity-language detection, an incomplete\n  personal pledge, and a malformed borrower self-registration ref) --\n  none of which ever reach a human -- every scenario's actual\n  disposition and violation `:basis` inspected directly against the\n  design before landing.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Option | Verdict | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| Model equity/investment alongside lending | ❌ | Explicit owner instruction: V1 is lending only. `equity-language-detected-violations` structurally blocks any attempt to smuggle equity language in |\n| Register under an existing/new ISIC financial-services code | ❌ | This actor is a cross-cutting matching/auxiliary layer, not an industry vertical; the relevant financial-services codes are already claimed by sibling actors and this actor does not itself grant credit, factor receivables, or hold deposits |\n| A single uniform lender-safeguard set (no institutional/individual split) | ❌ | Individual lenders carry materially different regulatory risk (貸金業法's 「業として」threshold) than licensed institutions; a single check set would be either too lax for individuals or too strict for licensed banks |\n| Treat the individual-lender loan-count threshold as a hard legal line | ❌ | No such bright line exists in the statute this actor cites; documenting it honestly as a conservative proxy avoids implying unearned legal certainty |\n| Live HTTP integration into `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami`'s self-registration registry | ❌ (deferred) | Out of scope for V1 per the task's explicit boundary; reference-field well-formedness is the V1 substitute, documented as such |\n| A `kernels/gate.cljc` WASM safety-kernel twin (following `credit.governor`'s pattern) | ❌ | Explicit V1 scope boundary (task instruction: no WASM twin); `factoring.governor`'s idiomatic-`.cljc`, no-kernel posture is the followed precedent instead |\n| A single actuation (record only, no separate tranche-release) | ❌ | The design specifies staged/tranche-based capital release gated on milestone evidence -- a single actuation cannot express \"release only after evidence of progress,\" the mechanism connecting the personal pledge to the disbursement schedule |\n| See `cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger`'s own ADR-0001 Alternatives table for further build-level decisions | -- | (auxiliary-boundary rationale, safeguard design, distinctive-check rationale, no-live-integration deferral, etc.) |\n\n## References\n\n- `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami` ADR-0013 (`docs/adr/0013-open-business-self-registration.md`)\n- `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami` ADR-0028 (`docs/adr/0028-ma-matching-deal-flow.md`)\n- `90-docs/adr/2607061700-cloud-itonami-vc-fund-blueprint.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607141700-cloud-itonami-isic-6493-factoring-actor.edn`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6492` (`credit.*`, the closest\n  single-application-entity Store/ground-truth-affordability-recompute\n  template)\n- `cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (the\n  authoritative repo-level architecture record for this actor)\n- https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger\n"}]
